So, i've seen people posting on here asking how to apply this patch or
that patch, and i figured i would learn to do the same. In the end, i
created an executable for windows tty with 8 patches applied (and they
all seem to be working). I choose patches that wouldn't affect gameplay
and hopefully will be save/bones compatible (i can't guarantee this at
the moment, maybe someone else can or i'll look into it later). It was
an exercise in patching/merging, and one that i think other people
would benefit from as well.

Patches applied:

1. Paranoid Quit
when enabled, Requires you to type "yes" instead of just "y" to quit.
http://bilious.homelinux.org/?44

2. Show buc
Adds an option to always show uncursed-status
http://bilious.homelinux.org/?198

3. Dump Character
Enables you to automatically dump certain data on the (most likely)
premature death of your character to a file.
http://bilious.homelinux.org/?40

4. While Helpless
Adds different messages to death reason, if you die while busy doing
something else.
http://bilious.homelinux.org/?12

5. Menucolors
Allows the user to define in what color menus are shown.
http://bilious.homelinux.org/?11

6. Statuscolors
Customizable coloring for the status (bottom) lines
http://bilious.homelinux.org/?142

7. Extinct & showborn v1.0
Show extinct and number of created monsters at the end of game.
http://bilious.homelinux.org/?43

8. Sortloot
Item lists can be sorted alphabetically by description when you loot or
apply containers or pick up something.
http://bilious.homelinux.org/?42


You can get the patched binary and sample config file here:
http://www.gigasize.com/get.php/92316/nethack-3.4.3-patched.zip

